            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0327" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.512351/275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marriner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-02T11:00:00+01:00">October 2, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 2—7:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>842. My 840, October 1, 6 p.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d208-f1"/> The decree
                    promulgating double taxation convention, dated yesterday appears in today’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Journal Officiel</hi> making the convention effective as
                    of January 1, 1936.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
